# AI-Powered Code Review GitHub Assistant

A production-grade GitHub App that automatically reviews every pull request using GPT-4o and posts inline comments directly on the PR — just like a human reviewer.

![TypeScript](https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-5.x-blue)
![Node.js](https://img.shields.io/badge/Node.js-18+-green)
![React](https://img.shields.io/badge/React-18-blue)
![GPT-4o](https://img.shields.io/badge/GPT--4o-OpenAI-purple)
![MongoDB](https://img.shields.io/badge/MongoDB-Atlas-green)
![Redis](https://img.shields.io/badge/Redis-Upstash-red)

---

## What It Does

When a pull request is opened on any connected GitHub repository:

1. GitHub sends a webhook to your Express server
2. Server verifies the HMAC-SHA256 signature and returns 200 immediately
3. Job is pushed to a Redis queue (prevents duplicates, handles retries)
4. Worker picks up the job, fetches the PR diff via GitHub API
5. Sends the diff to GPT-4o with a structured prompt
6. Posts inline review comments back to the PR
7. Saves the review to MongoDB
8. Dashboard updates with score, summary, and comment breakdown

---

## Architecture

```
GitHub PR opened
      │
      ▼
Express /webhook  ← HMAC-SHA256 verified
      │  Returns 200 immediately (async decoupling)
      │  Redis idempotency check (deliveryId)
      ▼
Redis Queue (Bull)
      │  Job: { repoFullName, prNumber, installationId, deliveryId }
      ▼
Worker (in-process for dev / AWS Lambda for prod)
      │  1. GitHub App auth (installation token)
      │  2. Fetch PR diff + file list in parallel
      │  3. Call GPT-4o → structured JSON review
      │  4. Post inline comments to PR via GitHub API
      │  5. Save review to MongoDB
      ▼
MongoDB Atlas  ←→  React Dashboard (Vite)
```

### Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| Return 200 before processing | GitHub retries if no 2xx in 10s. GPT-4o takes 15-30s. Without this, every review triggers duplicates. |
| Redis idempotency (deliveryId) | GitHub retries failed webhooks. We store delivery ID in Redis (24h TTL) to skip duplicates. |
| `crypto.timingSafeEqual` for HMAC | Regular string comparison leaks timing info. This prevents brute-force attacks on the webhook secret. |
| Bull queue with exponential backoff | If OpenAI or GitHub is down, jobs retry automatically (3s, 6s, 12s delays). |
| `response_format: json_object` | Guarantees valid JSON from GPT-4o — no regex parsing, no malformed responses. |
| MongoDB for reviews | Each review has a variable-length comments array. Document model fits naturally vs SQL. |
| In-process worker (dev) | Simpler local setup — no separate process needed. Use Lambda version for production. |

